^{2}+(y-8)^{2}=64" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519686 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519686 1083 #uuid "30e03e58-9723-53bc-8602-1ba18cff8fde" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519687 1068 #edb/ref 17592186519714 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519687 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519687 1071 "![](images/56/56e82ecf0aa2a54d7281882c095f3c2b081f719cf3398be20155301d0f0361a0.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-9,0)$ and $(9,0)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519687 1072 #uuid "31669fee-6340-55d5-a19f-a1a86dd81325" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519687 1074 "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-9,0)$ and $Y(9,0),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{((-9)-9)^2+(0-0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-18)^2+(0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{324+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{324} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{18}{2}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{-9+9}{2},\\frac{0+0}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=9$ and center $(a,b)=(0,0),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & =(9)^2 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519688 1068 #edb/ref 17592186519698 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519688 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519688 1071 "![](images/95/95467ab2e67bc1e188a5783ef201859c4e1216f071d6dc21b44adafcba8195c4.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-5,-4)$ and $(-1,2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519688 1072 #uuid "3d3ac566-19a8-54d2-a32a-fff15a573dbb" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519688 1074 "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-5,-4)$ and $Y(-1,2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{((-5)-(-1))^2+((-4)-2)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^2+(-6)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 13} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{13}}{2}=\\sqrt{13}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{-5+(-1)}{2},\\frac{-4+2}{2})=(-3,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{13}$ and center $(a,b)=(-3,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{13})^2 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519689 1068 #edb/ref 17592186519701 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519689 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519689 1071 "![](images/4a/4afda0c1af30967941c20c9f70ce926a04e029eedfa605eb3c20d62af8303947.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-9,-1)$ and $(3,-1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519689 1072 #uuid "3e71d13b-143e-5100-ac38-b145c988b060" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519689 1074 "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-9,-1)$ and $Y(3,-1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{((-9)-3)^2+((-1)-(-1))^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^2+(0)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{12}{2}=6.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2})=(\\frac{-9+3}{2},\\frac{-1+(-1)}{2})=(-3,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=6$ and center $(a,b)=(-3,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2 & =r^2 \\\\ (x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & =(6)^2 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519690 1075 #edb/ref 17592186519684 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519690 1075 #edb/ref 17592186519685 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519690 1075 #edb/ref 17592186519697 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519690 1075 #edb/ref 17592186519709 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519690 1075 #edb/ref 17592186519718 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519690 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519690 1077 "selection" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519690 1078 #edb/ref 17592186519709 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519690 1079 #uuid "3f2dd7ee-0390-5e7d-b56a-bdb4d7b3a503" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519691 1080 "(x+4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" 13194139535583 17592186045443 true] [17592186519691 1082 #edb/ref 17592